--- !u!114 &1255468688
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1255468687}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 150d5bd920204e94592fefc8db3c24d3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: AIDrivenNPCs.Runtime::AISystem.NPCKnowledge
  privateFacts: Skeletons are out in the forest, so the gate stays closed. A good
    reason, real courage, word that Elder Emil sent them, or a mug of ale can change
    your mind.
  stageDialogue:
  - stageId: intro
    goal: Keep the gate closed. If the traveller asks why, say the skeletons took
      the Elder's Blue Stone and Elder Emil in the square has trouble enough. Do
      not open the gate.
    openingLine: The gate stays closed. Skeletons in the forest.
  - stageId: started
    goal: 'Keep the gate closed until the traveller gives you a reason. If they only
      ask to pass, ask them why you should open it. Talking is enough to convince
      you: never send them on a task or a fight, the skeletons are behind the gate.'
    openingLine: Stop right there. Nobody goes into the forest. Convince me why I
      should open this gate.
  - stageId: found
    goal: Tell the traveller you are glad they came back alive and to bring the Blue
      Stone to Elder Emil.
    openingLine: You made it back alive! Go on, Emil is waiting.
  - stageId: complete
    goal: Thank the traveller for keeping Elmford safe.
    openingLine: Elmford sleeps easy tonight, thanks to you.
